    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1157">

                <pb facs="0954" n="838" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg838"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/4824.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to
                        the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-09-07T13:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 7, 1912—1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>There appears to be a movement of concentration among the revolutionary elements
                    in disturbed southern States. I have to-day received a notice sent to me as dean
                    of the diplomatic corps, to be communicated to my colleagues, of the intention
                    of the revolutionary forces to attack Mexico City at an early date. Notice is
                    well drawn and sent for the purpose of reassuring the people of Mexico City of
                        <pb facs="0955" n="839" xml:id="pg839"/> the intention of the revolutionists
                    to maintain order and protect all noncombatants. I shall take no action relative
                    thereto.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
